# {{.vars.name}} Documentation

## Overview

{{.vars.name}} is a command-line tool for {{.vars.description | default "managing your workflow"}}.

## Commands

### init

Initialize a new project:

```bash
{{.vars.name}} init
```

### run

Run a target:

```bash
{{.vars.name}} run [target]
{{.vars.name}} run build --parallel 4
{{.vars.name}} run test --dry-run
```

### list

List available targets:

```bash
{{.vars.name}} list
{{.vars.name}} list --all
```

### config

Manage configuration:

```bash
{{.vars.name}} config show
{{.vars.name}} config set key value
```

## Configuration

Configuration can be specified via:

1. Command-line flags
2. Config file (`~/.{{.vars.name}}.yaml`)
3. Environment variables

